# Motorhead body v1: Kobra X3 (car 01), Base body (09-remaster 9.22 phase 6, #179). Game-space
# metres, x to the right, y up, z forward. Colours `r,g,b` are the MYO face tags before the
# repaint. Design choices unless marked [O].
#
# [O] cage 213 v / 248 p (213 welded), 44 open edges, 2 edges on more than 2 faces, 207/213
# mirror twins (the six without one are the tail panel's corners, 4 mm off: x -0.233 / 0.237,
# -0.352 / 0.356, -0.706 / 0.710); 130 edges under 10 deg, 36 at 10-20, 261 over 20; edge min
# 0.042 median 0.302 m. Box x +-1.090, y 0.229..1.277, z -2.055..2.026.
# The two edges on more than 2 faces are the mirror bases, 4 faces each (housing 124/125 and
# 130/131 with the fender 96/100 and the cowl 184/238), as on the Adder and the Python.
# The open edges are not only the underside: most are T-junctions (a long edge against two
# shorter ones) on the roof 101/102/107/108, the windscreen and its logo strip 60/61/66/67, the
# nose 158-162 / 208-216, the bonnet vents 170/224 and the sills 174/177/228/231.
# An olive wedge: paint 75 91 34 (86 faces), orange 192 78 0 (40: the spine over the rear
# window, the mirrors, the nose's lower half, the sills, the rear panel), white 255 255 255
# (24: the spine's sides and the stripes beside it, the sill stripe). 70 flat black 0 0 0
# faces: the arch tunnels 17-52, the rear wing 69-86 (stays as in the original until the Full
# body), the side scoops 87-92, the spine's front 6, the windscreen corners 59 / 65, the nose
# intake 122, the panel between the tail lamps 12, the rear valance 139 and the bonnet vents
# 169 / 170 / 223 / 224. Textured: Underred (the underside), Oklog2 61 64 67 (the logo strip
# over the windscreen), Ogflight 120 / 121, Ogblight 10 / 11.
Body bevel=0.015 segments=3 bevel_tol=0.001 smooth_deg=10 arch_step_deg=7.5 arch_clearance=0.035 arch_lip=0.02 drop=0

# Design choice (third pass): the rounded fold alone is a plate through flat facets, so the
# bonnet and the nose stayed flat between the folds. The fold row (the cage points on the
# bonnet-to-nose fold, |x| 0.245-0.589, y 0.707-0.810, z 1.592-1.744, the vents' tips included)
# rises 3 cm and the fenders' nose corners (|x| 0.843, y 0.848, z 1.466) 1.5 cm before the
# curved zones, so the fold grows to 27 deg and `round=0.35` spreads it into a dome over the
# bonnet and the nose, as in the cinematic render. 3.5 cm without the corners notched the
# fenders' silhouette at the nose; 2.5 cm was a flatter dome.
Push lo=0.2,0.69,1.58 hi=0.6,0.82,1.76 by=0,0.03,0
Push lo=0.75,0.8,1.4 hi=0.9,0.9,1.5 by=0,0.015,0

# Design choice (fifth pass, the user's request: a straight, smooth fender edge over the front
# wheels, raised like the cinematic render's humps). Over the front arch the fender's outer fold
# (chamfer to side, F: |x| 0.931 y 0.841 z 1.185, 0.929 0.825 1.314, 0.913 0.784 1.462) lay at or
# under the arch lip's circle (y 0.83 over the hub at z 1.25: the tyre, the 0.035 clearance and
# the 0.02 lip), so the lip broke through the fold and the edge read jagged; the skin over the
# arch was 2-6 cm thick. F rises 3.5-4.5 cm (most over the hub) and clears the lip by 4.3-5 cm;
# the top corners over it (T: |x| 0.866 0.860 0.843 at z 1.185 1.344 1.466) 1-2 cm, so each
# chamfer quad stays flat (its corners' rises cancel) and the fender humps over the wheel. The
# bonnet's edge (|x| 0.571-0.589) and the mirror base stay. With the stiff fender springs below,
# T at 2.5-4.5 cm and F at 3.5-5 cm made an 8 cm hump.
Push lo=0.86,0.905,1.18 hi=0.872,0.917,1.19 by=0,0.01,0
Push lo=0.855,0.882,1.338 hi=0.866,0.894,1.35 by=0,0.02,0
Push lo=0.837,0.857,1.46 hi=0.849,0.869,1.472 by=0,0.01,0
Push lo=0.925,0.835,1.18 hi=0.937,0.847,1.19 by=0,0.035,0
Push lo=0.923,0.819,1.308 hi=0.935,0.831,1.32 by=0,0.045,0
Push lo=0.907,0.778,1.456 hi=0.919,0.79,1.468 by=0,0.035,0

# [O] the mirror glass is the grey 146 146 146 quad on the back of each housing (118 / 119,
# |x| 0.888-1.090, y 0.896-0.983, z 0.510-0.558)
MirrorGlass rgb=146,146,146

# [O] glass is 75 92 107 (11 faces: windscreen 60 62 63 66 68, side windows 54 / 57, the rear
# window in two halves either side of the spine 53 55 / 56 58)
Glass rgb=75,92,107 frame=0.02 inset=0.015 tint=0.6

# [O] headlights: one Ogflight quad a side, tag 127 127 104 (120 / 121, |x| 0.254-0.818,
# y 0.371-0.571, z 1.816-2.026, n 0.35 0 0.94: a wide lens across the nose's corner); halo 0/1
# runs it from (0.818 0.489 1.816) to (0.254 0.42 2.026), rgb ff f8 99. Design choice: a
# reflector bowl with three bulbs and a daytime bar along its bottom edge.
Lamp from=127,127,104 frame=0.008 inset=0.03 tint=0.45 kind=reflector count=3 rows=1 pitch=0 bulb=0.014 led_inset=0.03
Led pts=0,0;0.95,0 repeat=1 step=0,0 style=bar width=0.025 margin=0 clip=0 halo=1
# [O] tail lights: one Ogblight quad a side, tag 127 0 0 (10 / 11, |x| 0.233-0.722, y 0.664-0.800,
# z -2.055..-2.026, n 0 0.21 -0.98); halo 2/3 runs from (0.716 0.753 -2.034) to (0.296 0.732
# -2.04), rgb ff 11 11. The lens is a trapezoid: its top edge level (y 0.800), its bottom edge
# rising 7 deg outwards (0.664 at |x| 0.352 to 0.706 at 0.710), and the LED frame lies along
# the bottom edge. Design choice: two level light bars, parallel to the top edge and the halo
# (rising 0.12 frame widths over the run cancels the slope; along the bottom edge they sloped
# against the car's lines and stopped halfway across the lens).
Lamp from=127,0,0 frame=0.012 inset=0.02 tint=0.55 kind=leds led_inset=0.03
Led pts=0,0.03;0.95,0.15 repeat=2 step=0,0.1 style=bar width=0.03 margin=0 clip=0 halo=1

# [O] flat black (0 0 0) openings that are not arch tunnels, the wing or the underside:
# - the nose intake 122 between the headlights (|x| < 0.254, y 0.371-0.469, z 2.026): honeycomb
Vent from=0,0,0 lo=0,0.36,2.0 hi=0.26,0.48,2.05 rgb=3,3,3 frame=0.01 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=hex radius=0.012 wall=0.003 blades=0
# - the panel between the tail lamps 12 (|x| < 0.356, y 0.664-0.800, z -2.055..-2.026): slats
Vent from=0,0,0 lo=0,0.65,-2.07 hi=0.36,0.81,-2.0 rgb=3,3,4 frame=0.01 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.02 width=0.006 blades=0 spine=0.01 tilt=0
# - the side scoops' back walls 89 / 92 (|x| 0.78-0.966, y 0.493-0.909, z -0.753..-0.516,
#   facing forward and up): slats
Vent from=0,0,0 lo=0.77,0.48,-0.76 hi=0.97,0.92,-0.5 rgb=3,3,5 frame=0.01 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.03 width=0.01 blades=0 spine=0.01 tilt=0
# - the bonnet vents 169 / 170 and 223 / 224 (|x| 0.319-0.571, y 0.707-0.898, z 0.999-1.744):
#   louvres
Vent from=0,0,0 lo=0.3,0.7,0.98 hi=0.58,0.9,1.75 rgb=3,3,6 frame=0.008 inset=0.025 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.025 width=0.008 blades=0 spine=0.01 tilt=0
# - the orange lower nose under each headlight 161 / 214 (|x| 0.254-0.818, y 0.229-0.407,
#   z 1.817-2.026, n 0.35 0 0.94: angled back across the nose corner). Design choice after the
#   cinematic render of the Kobra X3 (#179, second pass), which has a pair of intakes there: a
#   panel 4.5 cm in from the face's edges, recessed with a honeycomb and one upright blade, so
#   it reads as two slots. Slats run along game x and poked out of this angled face at its
#   outer end.
Panel from=192,78,0 lo=0.3,0.2,1.8 hi=0.83,0.42,2.05 frame=0.045 rgb=4,4,1
Vent from=4,4,1 lo=0.3,0.2,1.8 hi=0.83,0.42,2.05 rgb=3,3,7 frame=0.006 inset=0.035 tint=0.5 kind=hex radius=0.012 wall=0.003 blades=1

# [O] The front fenders are a box of crisp facets (top 151 / 180, a 45 deg chamfer 146 / 185 and the
# side 147 / 186, folds 40-54 deg) that fan out at the nose corner into 148 / 150 / 181 / 187
# (folds 13-25 deg, and 40 between 148 and 150), where the chamfer fades into the nose. Unlike
# the other cars' fenders these are creases, not a Gouraud fan (only 36 cage edges at 10-20 deg,
# the fewest). The Classic body shades them round all the same, and the cinematic render of the
# Kobra X3 is round humps over the wheels, a bonnet and nose rolled over the stripe and rounded
# rear quarters (#179, second pass). Design choice: two curved zones over the paint, the white
# stripes and the orange (each face keeps its colour), every fold up to 60 deg rounded:
# - front: the fenders' top, chamfer and nose corner (|x| 0.55-0.915, z 0.6-1.9, y to 0.96
#   since the fifth pass, below; the vertical sides over the arch, |x| 0.93, stay out: rounded into the arch
#   lips they made 8 non-manifold edges there) and the bonnet and nose over the stripe (|x| <
#   0.6, z 1.15-2.05). The nose's side faces (212 / 213 / 216 on the right) stay out too: cut by the zone, the
#   lower nose's edge to them got cut points a hair off the line, which the panel above threw
#   out of the face as spikes.
# - rear: the rear fenders, the deck beside the spine and the tail (|x| 0.3-1.0, z < -0.75;
#   the spine, |x| 0.24, stays a ridge).
# The bonnet vents' black faces 169 / 223 are in the zone too (third pass, the user's request:
# their front tips (|x| 0.319, y 0.707, z 1.744) sit on the bonnet-to-nose fold, and as fixed
# outline corners they pinched the plate there at any `round` over 0.1; the vent recess finds
# the faired triangles by colour and box as before). The fender box is split in three so the
# black arch tunnels (17-46, centroid y under 0.76 or |x| under 0.8) stay out: the fenders' top
# (|x| 0.55-0.915, y 0.8+), their outer side (|x| 0.85+) and the nose corner 181 / 235 (|x|
# 0.7-0.8, y 0.7-0.8, z 1.6+); the bonnet box starts at z 1.3 so the tunnels' inner walls 25 /
# 43 (centroid z 1.27) stay out. Same paint faces as the two boxes before (checked face by
# face); 170 / 224 (the vents' rear halves, z under 1.3) stay flat under the cowl.
# `round=0.35`: 0.1 left the bonnet-to-nose fold (22 deg at z 1.744, 158-162 / 208-216 to the
# bonnet) a visible crease between two flat panels, which read concave next to the cinematic
# render's domed bonnet and nose; 0 dented the bonnet. The zone step
# moves the left headlight's top edge across weld cells: 1-3 more 3-face edges there (5, 6, 7
# at a step of 0.026, 0.025, 0.024), where the cage already has one; no crack in close-ups.
# Fifth pass (the user's request): the fenders' top 180 / 234 (centroid y 0.900) had stayed out
# of the 0.895 box, a flat facet pinned with the chamfer between two creases, so the boxes reach
# y 0.96 (only 180 / 234 join; the mirror faces stay out by z), and `round` is per box: 0.35 on
# the bonnet and the nose corner, 0.12 on the fenders' boxes. With 0.35 the fenders became one
# plane from the top to the side fold and sagged 5-8 cm under the cage over the arch; as their
# own zone at 0.1 they met the bonnet in a crease along the vents. One plate keeps that seam
# smooth; the points on both take the stiff springs, so the bonnet beside the vents' tips sits
# up to 9 cm higher than the soft plate left it, near the cage there.
Smooth from=75,91,34;255,255,255;192,78,0;0,0,0 lo=0,0.45,1.3;0.55,0.8,0.6;0.85,0.55,0.6;0.7,0.7,1.6 hi=0.6,0.92,2.05;0.915,0.96,1.9;0.915,0.96,1.9;0.8,0.8,1.9 max_deg=60 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.35;0.12;0.12;0.35
Smooth from=75,91,34;255,255,255;192,78,0 lo=0.3,0.4,-2.1 hi=1.0,1.01,-0.75 max_deg=60 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.1

# Every edge cut and every face remeshed at 4 cm, like the other base bodies.
# `seams=1` (#387, as the Avalanche's, #177): [O] the original meets a long edge with two or more
# shorter ones in places (T-junctions); cutting the open edges at those corners first closes the
# seam. Mesh check, open edges 5,244 -> 5,039, no new defect.
Refine step=0.04 seams=1

# Design choice (fourth pass, the user's request): the fenders' outer flank between the arch's
# front lip and the headlight's corner (faces 242 / 199 on the right: |x| 0.82-0.93, y 0.58-0.79,
# z 1.46-1.82) leaned in at its bottom (n y -0.14), so from the front the silhouette had a dent
# halfway between the fender's corner and the lamp. The refined cage bulges out by up to 5 cm
# there: full from |x| 0.85 out, peaking at y 0.65 and z 1.62 (the arch's front corner), none at
# the white stripe's bottom (y 0.45), over the fender's top (y 0.85), behind z 1.3 or at the
# headlight's corner (z 1.80), so the lamp and its housing stay put. 3 cm only straightened the
# dent. Mesh check unchanged (non-manifold 6). Rounding the side panels round the arch in the
# curved zone was tried and dropped: the panel behind the arch (237) sagged into a pillow, and
# the strips over the arch's top (197 / 199) made 3-7 non-manifold slivers against the arch lip
# at every zone step from 0.022 to 0.026.
Warp by=0.05,0,0 x=0.7,0;0.85,1 y=0.45,0;0.65,1;0.85,0 z=1.3,0;1.62,1;1.80,0
